{
    "background_story": "Solomon was a reclusive musicologist with a passion for the works of Frederick Delius. He spent most of his life studying the British composer's oeuvre, pouring over scores and manuscripts in search of hidden patterns and themes. As he delved deeper into Delius's music, Solomon became increasingly obsessed with the idea of recreating the composer's lost works. He spent years researching and experimenting, finally succeeding in reconstructing a previously unknown piano concerto. The discovery sent shockwaves through the classical music world, and Solomon was hailed as a genius. Despite his newfound fame, he remained devoted to Delius's music, continuing to uncover and interpret the composer's hidden gems. Solomon's dedication to Delius's legacy was a testament to the power of passion and scholarship.",
